{"id":"RISK-005","owner":"Brian","severity":"disclosed","trigger":"a future Rust syntax form outside SourceScanner's handled lexical states could leave a production path unwatched","requirement":"P1-R001","evidence":"docs/execution/m17-5-adversarial-findings.md:F-72","planned_phase":"M24","mitigation":"SourceScanner tracks strings, comments, raw strings and structural braces; alias/value closure across every registered oracle rejects known escapes. The remaining parser-versus-lexer gap is accepted under AM-17.11 and the qualifier is frozen","authority":"AM-17.11","state":"accepted"}
{"id":"RISK-006","owner":"Brian","severity":"disclosed","trigger":"a regression removing per-line coverage enforcement could let coarse scan omit a nonblank source region","requirement":"P1-R002","evidence":"docs/execution/m17-5-adversarial-findings.md:F-73","planned_phase":"M24","mitigation":"verify_coarse_scan independently reconstructs the blank-line block boundaries from the source and requires each block's range to equal its expected range, so an omitted or shortened nonblank region is refused. AM-17.15 classifies oracle coverage as suite rather than instrument, so this is exercised rather than recorded: the_coarse_oracle_refuses_a_scan_that_does_not_cover_the_source covers middle-block omission and both range shrinks, and deleting the reconstruction makes that test alone fail","authority":"AM-17.15","state":"mitigated"}
{"id":"RISK-007","owner":"Brian","severity":"disclosed","trigger":"a disabled-crash-point mutant survives when its derived killers assert recovery outcomes without asserting the injection fired","requirement":"P1-R015","evidence":"docs/execution/m17-5-adversarial-findings.md:F-74","planned_phase":"M24","mitigation":"AM-17.10 derives the killer column from the operator's observation kind, which constrains evidence kind but not oracle strength. Stage 1a predeclares mutants without executing them (AM-17.4: the 38 tests are unwritten), so a surviving P1-M049 is observable only at HAQP-1b, where haq mutants executes the plan and a survivor is recorded rather than argued","authority":"ADR-0021 stage 1b","state":"accepted"}
