{"in_scope":[{"subsystem":"ilrp","path":"crates/liminal-jurisdiction/src/ilrp.rs","sites":3}],"deferred":[{"path":"crates/liminal-daemon/src/runner.rs","sites":22,"reason":"graph transaction commits in the Phase 0 daemon; whether each fsynced txn.commit is a registrable boundary is a runtime design question, not a qualification one (M17.5 A05)"},{"path":"crates/liminal-jurisdiction/src/reconcile.rs","sites":4,"reason":"reconciliation commits outside the ILRP protocol steps the registry covers"},{"path":"crates/liminal-source/src/file.rs","sites":8,"reason":"atomic file replacement and directory fsync; the durable primitive ILRP is built on, not an ILRP step (F-47 A05 brought its fsync and atomic-rename sites into the census: 3 commit_if, 2 rename, 2 fsync; a crash leaves the old or the new file, never a partial one)"},{"path":"crates/liminal-daemon/src/session.rs","sites":2,"reason":"session state commits; same open question as runner.rs"},{"path":"crates/liminal-daemon/src/executor.rs","sites":1,"reason":"executor commit_if; same open question as runner.rs"},{"path":"crates/liminal-daemon/src/reactor.rs","sites":1,"reason":"reactor commit; same open question as runner.rs"},{"path":"crates/liminal-graph/src/owner.rs","sites":1,"reason":"existing workspace epoch commit relocated to EpochWriter::persist under AM-17.12/DG17.4; unchanged deferred classification, same open question as runner.rs"},{"path":"crates/liminal-cli/src/format.rs","sites":1,"reason":"M20 formatter replacement, quarantined under AM-17.2; its injection unwinds rather than aborting, so it is strictly weaker than a crash boundary"},{"path":"crates/liminal-graph/src/store/mod.rs","sites":2,"reason":"the store's single checksummed log append (P1-M022): a crash leaves a torn tail that recovery truncates to the longest checksummed prefix (prop_torn_tail_truncates_cleanly), not state to reconcile, so it is not a registrable boundary (AM-17.8; M17.5 F-46 A05 brought it into the census)"},{"path":"crates/liminal-daemon/src/crash.rs","sites":2,"reason":"the fault-injection recorder's fsync of its hit log: diagnostic state for crash-matrix evidence, not world state, so a crash mid-write loses a hit count and nothing recovery reconciles (M17.5 F-47 A05 brought fsync into the census)"},{"path":"crates/liminal-graph/src/store/log.rs","sites":7,"reason":"the checksummed append log's fsyncs (record, batch, directory): a crash leaves a torn tail that recovery truncates to the longest checksummed prefix (prop_torn_tail_truncates_cleanly), not state to reconcile (AM-17.8; F-47 A05)"},{"path":"crates/liminal-graph/src/store/snapshot.rs","sites":2,"reason":"the snapshot's fsync and atomic rename: a crash before the rename leaves the previous snapshot, after it the new one; either is a consistent state the log replays onto, nothing to reconcile (AM-17.8; F-47 A05)"}],"deferred_to":"M17.9","rationale":"ADR-0020 §5 requires exhaustive REGISTERED crash boundaries without stating the surface. AM-17.8 defines a registrable boundary as a point where a crash leaves state that recovery must RECONCILE. ILRP's eight protocol steps qualify. The runtime's ~30 other fsynced durable transitions are single checksummed log appends: a torn append is truncated to the longest checksummed prefix (liminal-graph store/log.rs, proven by prop_torn_tail_truncates_cleanly in crates/liminal-graph/tests/store.rs), so recovery is 'read the log' and there is nothing to reconcile. The deferred surface below is pinned by site count so this claim fails loudly if a new transition appears that is not a plain append."}
