15452	/// Run the five families and return their evidence rows plus per-family
15453	/// wall-clock timings.
15454	///
15455	/// The timings are returned SEPARATELY rather than embedded in the rows on
15456	/// purpose: the rows are the hashable artifact and must be a pure function of
15457	/// the seed and the code under test, while the timings are telemetry for the
15458	/// operator (M17.5 pass-2 #18).
15459	///
15460	/// The case-count guard is a separate function so its BOUNDARIES are testable:
15461	/// `>` -> `>=` at the safety limit can only be discriminated by a case that
15462	/// runs at exactly 10,000,000, which no test can afford. Extracting the
15463	/// predicate makes the boundary checkable in microseconds (M17.5 F-30).
15464	/// Reject a case count that is zero or beyond the safety limit.
15465	fn validate_case_count(cases: u64) -> Result<()> {
15466	    if cases == 0 {
15467	        anyhow::bail!("generated case count must be positive");
15468	    }
15469	    if cases > 10_000_000 {
15470	        anyhow::bail!("generated case count exceeds safety limit: {cases} > 10000000");
15471	    }
15472	    Ok(())
15473	}
