10026	/// Whether a declared anchor line contains anything a mutation can change
10027	/// (M17.5 F-33 / blind pass 1 A04, A06, A10).
10028	///
10029	/// Operator rules already existed, but only over a mutation's before/after text
10030	/// — i.e. only at stage 1b, where evidence exists. At 1a the packet's declared
10031	/// anchors were checked for POSITION and never for whether the line held any
10032	/// behaviour. Blind pass 1 walked in and found operators anchored to function
10033	/// signatures and enum variants.
10034	///
10035	/// This rejects exactly one thing: a line that DECLARES rather than does. A
10036	/// signature has no predicate to invert, no threshold to shift, no crash point
10037	/// to disable, and no ordering to perturb; whatever the operator, the mutation
10038	/// cannot be applied there, and a mutant that cannot be applied can never be
10039	/// killed while still inflating the denominator §3 counts.
10040	///
10041	/// It deliberately does NOT try to match operators to line contents. A first
10042	/// version did, and rejected three legitimate anchors: `NodeFlags(self.0 |
10043	/// other.0)` is a real inversion site, `if rev == inner.state.head` is a real
10044	/// staleness comparison, and `for entry in entries.flatten()` is a real
10045	/// ordering site. Guessing which token an operator needs produces false
10046	/// accusations against a mutation plan; "is this a declaration" does not.
10047	/// Whether a mutant is GOOD is the 1b runner's question.
10048	/// The aliases a `use` line introduces for the symbols it imports:
10049	/// `use std::fs::{rename as mv, remove_file};` yields `("rename", "mv")`.
10050	/// Blind-review follow-up (review of c455cdf): splitting the whole line on
10051	/// `" as "` mangled a brace group into an alias like `mv, remove_file}`, which
10052	/// matched nothing and reopened the evasion the alias scan closed.
10053	/// `line` with a leading item visibility removed: `pub`, `pub(crate)`,
10054	/// `pub(super)`, `pub(in crate::x)`. Unchanged when it carries none, and
10055	/// unchanged for an identifier that merely starts with those letters.
10056	fn without_visibility(line: &str) -> &str {
10057	    let trimmed = line.trim();
10058	    let Some(rest) = trimmed.strip_prefix("pub") else {
10059	        return trimmed;
10060	    };
10390	    }
10391	    None
10392	}
